        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Alinta Energy, Chow Tai Fook Enterprises\n- Places: Playford B Power Station, Curlew Island, Port Augusta, Point Lowly, West Wallabi Island, Wallabi Group, Houtman Abrolhos, Indian Ocean, mainland Australia\n- Topics: Mothballing and closure, ownership, location\n\nFacts:\n- Playford B Power Station was mothballed in 2012.\n- In October 2015, Alinta Energy announced the permanent closure of Playford B Power Station.\n- Alinta Energy is an Australian private company involved in generation, electricity retailing, and gas retailing.\n- Alinta Energy is owned by Hong Kong-based Chow Tai Fook Enterprises.\n- Curlew Island in South Australia lies between Port Augusta and Point Lowly.\n- Curlew Island is adjacent to Playford B Power Station.\n- West Wallabi Island is in the Wallabi Group of the Houtman Abrolhos.\n- West Wallabi Island lies in the Indian Ocean off the west coast of mainland Australia.",
